|#DCFCE7|Surface|
start
:read the source text\n`(q0 , <[] | 0 | [0,1]>)`;

|#DBEAFE|WPDA parser|
:try ALL FIVE category parsers\n(`language_struct.rs:17-112`);
:only `Config` succeeds ->\n`Cf(Q0, Tp([], Zero, [Zero, One]))`;

|#EDE9FE|E-graph injection|
:`__mettail_dovetail_add_config`\nadds one e-node per constructor;
:each `Vec(Sym)` field becomes\n`FieldOpaque(format!("{:?}", field))`\n(`dovetail_report.rs:1007-1010`);

|#EDE9FE|Set automaton|
:both left-hand sides are AC-free, so\n`compile_positional_segments` puts them in\nONE segment with ONE compiled automaton\n(`dovetail/src/rules.rs:437-466`);
:`batched_segment_matches` traverses the graph ONCE\nand demultiplexes hits back to their rule by `PatternId`\n(`dovetail/src/rules.rs:775-787`);

|#FCE7F3|Rule application|
if (head symbol under `Tp`) then (`Sym_Zero`)
  :**D_q0_0** matches with\n<latex>\sigma = \{L \mapsto [\,],\; R \mapsto [0,1]\}</latex>;
elseif (head symbol under `Tp`) then (`Sym_One`)
  :**D_q0_1** matches with the same\n<latex>L</latex> and <latex>R</latex> bindings;
else (neither)
  :no rule matches — the configuration\nis already a normal form;
  |#FEF3C7|Report|
  :`rule_firings` is EMPTY\n(pinned by `languages/tests/turing.rs:167-174`);
  stop
endif

|#FCE7F3|Rule application|
:instantiate the right-hand side and\n**MERGE** it with the matched class —\na rewrite is a UNION, not a replacement\n(`dovetail/src/rules.rs:804-807`);
:record the firing under the paper's own label\n`Turing::rewrite::D_q0_0`;

|#EDE9FE|Saturation|
:iterate to convergence. The merged class now holds BOTH\nthe pre- and the post-transition node, so re-matching\nproduces no new merge and saturation stops;

|#FEF3C7|Report|
:`dovetail_report_for` returns\n`rule_firings = [D_q0_0]`, `completeness = Complete`;

|#EDE9FE|Extraction|
:`funded_best` takes the 1-best derivation under the\ntropical semiring. `__weigh` is CONSTANT <latex>1.0</latex> here\nbecause `__is_fold_redex` is `false` for every op\n(`dovetail_report.rs:3923-3940`);

|#FEE2E2|Reconstruction|
:`dovetail_normal_term` calls\n`__mettail_dovetail_build_tape_d`;
:no arm exists for `Tape_Tp` or `Tape_shift_right` —\ntheir `FieldOpaque` children have no inverse;
:**fail closed**: `Err("... reconstruction ... failed (stuck term)")`;
stop

note right
  This is why the conformance suite proves the dynamics from
  RULE FIRINGS and not from a reconstructed normal form
  (`languages/tests/turing.rs:10-21`): the reduction happened,
  but this language's shapes cannot be read back out of the
  e-graph. The same non-invertibility makes the in-Rho backend
  reject the language: `repl/src/rho_backends.rs:16`.
